  "prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress was established in January 2019 with the purpose of investigating, studying, and making recommendations on modernizing Congress. The committee, which consists of twelve Members appointed by the Speaker and the minority leader, was given a year-long authorization to examine House operations and propose rules and procedures to promote a more efficient and modern Congress. The committee's areas of focus include rules, technology, staffing, and various other operational aspects. The committee has held several hearings, including one where Members presented their own ideas for reform, and has received funding for its operations. The committee is required to submit a final report to the House with its findings and recommendations, which must be approved by a majority of its members. The report must be made publicly available within House rules. The committee's work is focused on improving the functioning of Congress in the 21st century, with a particular emphasis on promoting efficiency, transparency, and inclusivity.",
  "scored_prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress was established in January 2019 with the purpose of investigating, studying, and making recommendations on modernizing Congress. The committee, which consists of twelve Members appointed by the Speaker and the minority leader, was given a year-long authorization to examine House operations and propose rules and procedures to promote a more efficient and modern Congress. The committee's areas of focus include rules, technology, staffing, and various other operational aspects. The committee has held several hearings, including one where Members presented their own ideas for reform, and has received funding for its operations. The committee is required to submit a final report to the House with its findings and recommendations, which must be approved by a majority of its members. The report must be made publicly available within House rules. The committee's work is focused on improving the functioning of Congress in the 21st century, with a particular emphasis on promoting efficiency, transparency, and inclusivity.",
  "score": 30.76923027744905,
  "answers": [
    "On January 4, 2019, the House established the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress by adopting Title II of H.Res. 6, the House rules package for the 116th Congress (2019-2020), on a 418-12 vote. The purpose of the select committee as stated in its authorizing resolution is \"to investigate, study, make findings, hold public hearings, and develop recommendations on modernizing Congress.\" Twelve Members, six from each party, have been selected by their leadership to serve on the select committee during its year-long investigation. The committee's authorizing resolution requires its membership to include two Members from the freshman class of the 116th Congress, two Members of the Rules Committee, and two Members of the Committee on House Administration. Funding for the select committee in the amount of $487,500 was provided through House adoption of H.Res. 245 on March 27, 2019. The committee has held four hearings to date, with additional meetings likely. Committee operations are scheduled to end on February 1, 2020. Any final report of the committee will be made public. Publication of the final report will require approval from at least two-thirds of the committee. Given that both parties are equally represented on the committee, some amount of bipartisan support will be needed to approve and publish the final report."
  ],
